<title>USA: Tele-Communications to lay off 2,500 employees.</title>
<headline>Tele-Communications to lay off 2,500 employees.</headline>
<dateline>ENGLEWOOD, Colo.</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tele-Communications Inc., the nation's largest cable television operator, said Thursday it will cut 2,500 employess, or nearly 7 percent of its work force, as it seeks to lower costs and reduce debt.</p>
<p>The Englewood, Colo.-based company said it would review all expenses not directly related to serving customers.</p>
<p>The company said the layoffs, which will come from corporate headquarters and field offices, will amount to 2,500 managers and employees.</p>
<p>The layoffs were larger than had been anticipated by Wall Street analysts, who were looking for a 5 percent cut.</p>
</text>
